# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained model artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# models/svs_model.pkl, models/model_metrics.json, and models/test_split.csv
# are intentionally NOT ignored here — see the tradeoff note below.
#
# Commit them (current choice) when:
#   - you want anyone who clones the repo to run the API immediately
#     without first running training/train.py
#   - the model file is small (this one is — a handful of small sklearn trees)
#   - you don't have a separate model registry / artifact store set up
#
# Ignore them instead when:
#   - the model file is large (tens/hundreds of MB)
#   - the dataset contains sensitive data you don't want baked into a
#     binary artifact in version control
#   - you have CI/CD that trains and publishes the model separately
#
# If you switch to the second approach later, uncomment:
#
# models/*.pkl
# models/model_metrics.json
# models/test_split.csv
